course: dictionary
lesson: 3982
title: Big words from space
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Galactic» comes from «galaxy», a huge group of stars, gas and dust held together by gravity. Our Milky Way is one galaxy. When you see galact in a word, think about stars and space.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The Sun takes about 230 million years to go once round the centre of the galaxy, a "galactic year".» The words centre of the galaxy tell you that a galactic year is one very long trip around the middle of a galaxy.
explain: Sometimes «galactic» means something different. «The bedroom was a galactic mess after the party.» No space is involved: it means enormous. Try the swap check. Could you say «a space mess»? No, so the meaning is huge, and the clues tell you which sense to use.
fact: Galactic means to do with a galaxy, a huge group of stars, gas and dust held together by gravity.
fact: Our Milky Way is a galaxy, so galactic can describe things across or inside it, such as the galactic centre.
fact: «A galactic year» is the time the Sun takes to go once round the centre of the galaxy: about 230 million years.
fact: Informally, «galactic» means enormous or huge in size or importance, as in «a galactic mess».
fact: Phrases you may meet: galactic scale, intergalactic travel (travel between galaxies), and galactic war in science fiction stories.
exercise: «The Sun takes about 230 million years to go once round the centre of the galaxy, a "galactic year".» What does galactic mean in this sentence? | Very tiny | Made of wood | *To do with a galaxy | Very cold
exercise: Ella says «a galactic mess» means a space mess. What does galactic mean here? | *Enormous, huge | Made of stars | Slightly damp | Quiet and calm
exercise: Which word means to do with a galaxy, a huge group of stars held together by gravity? | Garden | *Galactic | Gentle | Gravel
test: What does intergalactic mean? | Inside a garden | Very slow | *Between galaxies | Made of gas only
test: In a science book, what is «the galactic centre»? | A kind of rain | Our school playground | A type of cake | *The middle of a galaxy
exam: Which sentence uses galactic to mean enormous? | A galactic year is the Sun's trip round the galaxy. | Galactic describes things in space. | *The bedroom was a galactic mess after the party. | The galactic centre is in the middle of the galaxy.
